Z||000000||Hank is Here||11-05-2000||11:32 PM||||Modification:  shaving of driver's side rear view mirror and front body panel realignment:  applicable to all body styles and years of Fiero's<P>Tools:  no tools but an SUV is necessary  (in my case a Ford Explorer choose my car, maybe this could just be blamed on Firestone)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> <P>Assistance:  one other person is necessary, do not have a friend help with this one (a clueless female driver is preferred especially one that was in a fender bender last Wednesday:  clueless male drivers will do as well just as long as they are clueless)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> <P>Method:  On the day that you are gonig to your first Fiero event start the drive about 9 a.m. with parknig lights on.  Have SUV make a left turn about 15 feet in front a your Fiero while you are traveling about 20 mph. It is NECESSARY to have the SUV driver say I did not look in that direction, but usually do   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> <P>Results:  shaved off drivers mirror, cracked door panel, realigned fender and facia, misaligned front end steering<P>Approximate Modification time: 0.3 seconds<P>Guarantee:  this has a 100% non-satisfaction guarantee<P><BR>Mark Johnson <p>[This message has been edited by Hank is Here (edited 11-05-2000).]||||reg||8
